      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 91-year-old woman came to the hospital with vomiting, abdominal pain and absence of defaecation for 1 day. Her medical history listed atrial fibrillation for which she received acenocoumarol and digoxine. CT imaging of her abdomen revealed an intramural haematoma of the jejunum."},
